From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Smith-Denny <osde@microsoft.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 10:10:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] MdeModulePkg: Add Compatibility Mode Functionality

[ouroBIOS: commit 8b0cd75a15be of MrChromebox's edk2, as it is]

This commit adds the functions that will comprise
compatibility mode, but they are not called yet.

Compatibility mode enables running bootloaders
and Option ROMs that violate memory protections and
would otherwise crash the system.

This is a living list, based on observed behaviors of
modules, that is is expected to be updated to maintain
compatibility with shipped applications.

The current heuristic that is used to enter compatibility
mode is when an EFI_APPLICATION is loaded that does not
have the NX_COMPAT DLL_CHARACTERISTIC set. There is industry
consensus on using this flag to indicate support for running
with memory protections enabled. edk2 already sets this flag
on all binaries with 4K section alignment.

When compatibility mode is entered, the following occurs:
- The memory attributes protocol is uninstalled. This has been
  observed to be incorrectly used to set all of a bootloader's
  memory as NX, then attempt to set a non-page aligned size to
  executable which fails, and the bootloader jumps to an NX page.
- Map page 0 as RWX. It has been observed that bootloader's can
  attempt to directly access this page to try to find legacy boot
  structures.
- Map the legacy boot writeback region as RWX (if this is part of
  system memory) as it has been observed that bootloaders attempt
  to directly access this region to look for legacy structures.
- Allocate all new memory as RWX. It has been observed that bootloaders
  will attempt to chainload another application and not set the region
  as executable.
- Image memory protections will not be applied, for the same reason.
- An event is fired for any platform code that would like to take
  action.

Signed-off-by: Oliver Smith-Denny <osde@microsoft.com>
(cherry picked from commit 3d6368bc5edca41efbf06ab9d19a34b11770c45d)
---
